title: Move 1 kickoff plans landed (29 Arky, 30 Aegis); Aegis flags a critical custody claim before code
summary: |-
  Research 29 (Arky) covers:
  - the package scaffold: contracts, kernel, helper and a wrapper skeleton now; the GUI, local runner and mods later; voice not yet;
  - the kernel has no dependencies key, with fence and SEC tests;
  - 14 M1.0 probes ordered by spec risk;
  - a Windows CI matrix plus an install-deps rollup fix;
  - PR-0 to PR-5.

  Research 30 (Aegis) lists spec claims believed false before any code:
  - K1 (critical): macOS kernel-key custody "full" fails, because any same-user process can run the helper. The fix is a signed Node SEA kernel plus an XPC peer check, or custody partial.
  - K2: presence prompts can be phished by a same-user process.
  - K3: no WFP job-object condition exists, and filter creation needs admin.
  - K4: the Windows wording should name the Passport KSP, not the Platform provider.
  - K5: unlocks live in the helper, not in kernel memory.
  - K6: the pipe PID check adds nothing.
  - K7: the launch token may persist in browser history.
  - K8: capture exclusion needs a native panel.

  Aegis also wrote ten probes, S29-01..10. Founder decisions pending:
  - a Developer ID provisioning profile for <TEAM>.gnomon.helper;
  - Windows hardware or a VM;
  - notarization now or later;
  - Windows code signing;
  - the Windows helper language (Arky proposes Rust);
  - K1 fix (a) or (b);
  - Node >=24 for Gnomon only.
